LESSON 2 - Visual Basic.NET and Visual Studio 
- I learned about the .NET Programming Languages, Visual Basic.NET, C#, F#. and Visual C++.
- .NET is Microsoft's software development platform.
- The two main components of .NET are Class Library and Runtime
- Class Library: contains pre-written code programmer to develop the .NET applications
- Runtime: Runs and manage .NET applications by providing services such as code execution, memory management, and exception handling.
  

Lesson 3 - How to code a complete Windows Form Application
- I learned about the form designers and toolbox windows. 
- Form Designer: Shows the GUI of a form, and allows you to visually design the GUI of a form.
- Toolbox: Contains the controls you use to design the GUI and you use the window to add controls to the interface of a form.
- I learned about the Properties Window
- Properties: Display the properties and events of a the selectec control, allows you to change the appearance and behavior of the selected control
- Properties EXs: Name, Text, Font, BackColor
- I learned how to use the Solution Explorer Window and the Code Editor Window
- I learned how to create the event-handler for the Calculate button and the event-handler for the Exit Button
